@startuml
title I2CIP - Core Device Model and Addressing

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
hide empty members

package "I2CIP Namespace" {
  enum i2cip_errorlevel_t {
    I2CIP_ERR_NONE
    I2CIP_ERR_SOFT
    I2CIP_ERR_HARD
  }

  enum i2cip_state_pin_t {
    PIN_OFF
    PIN_ON
    PIN_UNDEF
  }
}

package "Addressing and Bus Control" {
  object FQA {
    +createFQA(wire, mux, bus, addr): i2cip_fqa_t
    +beginWire(wire): bool
    +fqaToString(fqa): String
    --
    {static} wires: TwoWire*[1..2]
    {static} wiresBegun: bool[]
  }

  object MUX {
    +pingMUX(fqa): bool
    +pingMUX(wire, module): bool
    +setBus(fqa): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +setBus(wire, module, bus): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +resetBus(fqa): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +resetBus(wire, module): i2cip_errorlevel_t
  }
}

package "Core Device Model" {
  class InputGetter {
    +get(args: void*): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +failGet(): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +getLastRX(): unsigned long
    +cacheToString(): const char*
  }

  class OutputSetter {
    +set(value: void*, args: void*): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +reset(args: void*): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +failSet(value: void*): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +getLastTX(): unsigned long
    +valueToString(): const char*
  }

  class Device {
    -fqa: i2cip_fqa_t
    -id: i2cip_id_t
    -timeout: uint16_t
    -ready: bool
    -input: InputGetter*
    -output: OutputSetter*
    --
    +get(args: void*): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +set(value: void*, args: void*): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +ping(resetbus: bool=true, setbus: bool=true): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +pingTimeout(setbus: bool=true, resetbus: bool=true): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +read/write register helpers...
  }

  class "InputInterface<G,A>" as InputInterface {
    -cache: G
    -argsA: A
    +get(args: void*): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +getCache(): const G&
    +get(dest: G&, args: A): i2cip_errorlevel_t
  }

  class "OutputInterface<S,B>" as OutputInterface {
    -value: S
    -argsB: B
    +set(value: void*, args: void*): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +getValue(): S
    +set(value: S, args: B): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +resetFailsafe(): void
  }

  class "IOInterface<G,A,S,B>" as IOInterface

  class EEPROM {
    -readBuffer: char[257]
    {static} _failsafe_set: bool
    {static} _failsafe: char[256]
    {static} _failsafe_b: uint16_t
    --
    +readContents(...): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +overwriteContents(...): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +clearContents(...): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +get(dest: char*&, args: uint16_t): i2cip_errorlevel_t
    +set(value: const char* const&, args: uint16_t): i2cip_errorlevel_t
  }
}

InputInterface --|> InputGetter
OutputInterface --|> OutputSetter
IOInterface --|> InputInterface
IOInterface --|> OutputInterface
EEPROM --|> Device
EEPROM --|> IOInterface

Device ..> MUX : set/reset bus
Device ..> FQA : address segmentation

note right of FQA
FQA (Fully Qualified Address) is a packed 16-bit route key:
- wire segment (physical I2C controller index)
- module segment (MUX/module number)
- bus segment (MUX channel)
- addr segment (7-bit peripheral address)

createFQA() validates each segment before packing.
fqaToString() is primarily diagnostics/debug formatting.
end note

note right of MUX
MUX is the bus-path switch layer.

Primary responsibilities:
- ping switch presence
- set active downstream channel
- reset switch channel(s)

Fake MUX / fake bus values are intentionally supported
to model direct-wire devices that bypass multiplexing.
end note

note bottom of Device
Device is the transport-centric base class:
- Owns immutable FQA identity and logical device ID
- Exposes common read/write/register primitives
- Centralizes ping/readiness/recovery behavior
- Delegates typed I/O semantics to InputGetter/OutputSetter

State model:
ready=false after failures, then lazy re-begin on next operation.
end note

note right of InputGetter
Type-erased input endpoint used by Device::get().

failGet() routes through a sentinel argument to request
default/reset behavior from typed InputInterface<G,A>.
end note

note right of OutputSetter
Type-erased output endpoint used by Device::set().

reset()/failSet() use sentinel argument/value combinations
to invoke default/failsafe behavior in OutputInterface<S,B>.
end note

note bottom of InputInterface
InputInterface<G,A> adds typed caching and argument replay:
- cache stores last successful GET payload
- argsA stores last effective read arguments
- first-call default args supplied by getDefaultA()

Pattern: stateless transport + stateful typed interface.
end note

note bottom of OutputInterface
OutputInterface<S,B> adds typed output history:
- value stores last successful SET value
- argsB stores last effective write arguments
- getDefaultB()/resetFailsafe() define recovery defaults

This enables repeat-write and failsafe semantics.
end note

note right of EEPROM
EEPROM is both:
1) A normal I2CIP Device
2) A typed IOInterface<char*, uint16_t, const char*, uint16_t>

It is used as:
- module metadata source (JSON-ish config string)
- persistent key data store

Implementation performs bounded page writes and
pingTimeout() polling between writes for write-cycle completion.
end note

@enduml
